use std
into layout.amni
lang amni
Amni-Drive's driver-ergonomic cockpit layout, circular/hex/capsule pod geometry, and button-placement engine. All coordinates and sizes are 32-bit floats in logical pixels.
Struct `Rect` holds `x`, `y`, `w`, and `h` as 32-bit floats.
Struct `Circle` holds `cx`, `cy`, and `r` as 32-bit floats.
Struct `HitButton` holds `id` as a 32-bit integer, `rect` as a `Rect`, and `primary` as a boolean.
Struct `Pod` holds `kind` as a 32-bit integer (0 map, 1 media, 2 speed, 3 weather, 4 apps, 5 widgets), `shape` as a 32-bit integer (0 rect, 1 circle, 2 hex, 3 capsule), `rect` as a `Rect`, `circle` as a `Circle`, `safe_rect` as a `Rect`, and `chamfer` as a 32-bit float.
Struct `CockpitPlan` holds `screen_w` and `screen_h` as 32-bit floats, `layout_id` as a 32-bit integer, `dock_rect` as a `Rect`, `stage_rect` as a `Rect`, `portrait` as a boolean, `dock_bottom` as a boolean, `buttons` as a growable list of `HitButton`, and `pods` as a growable list of `Pod`.
Function `make_rect` takes `x`, `y`, `w`, and `h` as 32-bit floats and returns a `Rect`.
Function `rects_overlap` takes two `Rect` values `a` and `b` and returns true if their interiors strictly overlap by more than 0.5 pixels on both axes.
Function `rect_inside` takes `inner` and `outer` as `Rect` values and returns true if `inner` lies inside `outer` within 0.5 pixel tolerance on all four edges and has positive width and height.
Function `inscribe_circle` takes a `Rect` `r` and returns a `Circle` centered in `r` with radius equal to half of the smaller of `r.w` and `r.h`.
Function `circle_safe_rect` takes a `Circle` `c` and returns the chord-safe inner `Rect` centered at `c.cx`, `c.cy` with width and height equal to `c.r * 1.4142`.
Function `make_pod` takes `kind` and `shape` as 32-bit integers and `r` as a `Rect`, and returns a `Pod`. When `shape` is 1 (circle), set `circle` to `inscribe_circle` of `r`, `safe_rect` to `circle_safe_rect` of that circle, and `chamfer` to 0. When `shape` is 2 (hex), set `chamfer` to `min(r.w, r.h) * 0.08` clamped between 12 and 28, and inset `safe_rect` by `chamfer * 0.55` on all sides. When `shape` is 3 (capsule), set `chamfer` to `min(min(r.w, r.h) * 0.30, 56.0)` and inset `safe_rect` horizontally by `min(r.w * 0.08, chamfer * 0.55)` and vertically by 10. Otherwise (rect), `safe_rect` equals `r` and `chamfer` is 0.
Function `compute_cockpit` takes `screen_w`, `screen_h`, `min_hit`, `gutter`, and `pad` as 32-bit floats, `layout_id` as a 32-bit integer (0 twin chrono, 1 solar orbit, 2 orb center, 3 horizon dials, 4 hex cockpit, 5 capsule deck, 6 asym triptych, 7 tri cockpit, 8 split, 9 full map), `dock_mode` as a 32-bit integer (0 auto driver rail, 1 bottom dock, 2 right-hand-drive rail), and `swap_map_media` as a boolean, returning a `CockpitPlan`.
First decide orientation: `portrait` is true when `screen_h` is greater than `screen_w * 1.05`. `dock_bottom` is true when `portrait` is true or `dock_mode` is 1.
Compute the driver-ergonomic dock and stage rectangles:
- When `dock_bottom` is true: `dock_h` is `max(min_hit + 14.0, 72.0)` clamped to at most `screen_h * 0.18`. `dock_rect` sits along the bottom edge `(pad, screen_h - dock_h - pad, screen_w - 2.0 * pad, dock_h)`. `stage_rect` fills `(pad, pad, screen_w - 2.0 * pad, screen_h - dock_h - 2.0 * pad - gutter)`.
- When `dock_bottom` is false: `dock_w` is `max(min_hit + 16.0, 78.0)` clamped to at most `screen_w * 0.14`. If `dock_mode` is 2 (right-hand drive), `dock_rect` sits on the right edge `(screen_w - dock_w - pad, pad, dock_w, screen_h - 2.0 * pad)` and `stage_rect` fills `(pad, pad, screen_w - dock_w - 2.0 * pad - gutter, screen_h - 2.0 * pad)`. Otherwise (left-hand drive default), `dock_rect` sits on the left edge `(pad, pad, dock_w, screen_h - 2.0 * pad)` and `stage_rect` fills `(pad + dock_w + gutter, pad, screen_w - dock_w - 2.0 * pad - gutter, screen_h - 2.0 * pad)`.
Place the six driver-priority buttons inside `dock_rect` with ids 1 (NAV), 2 (MEDIA), 3 (APPS), 4 (VOICE, marked primary true), 5 (LAYOUT), and 6 (SETTINGS):
- Along the dock's long axis, divide the available span (`long_span - 5.0 * btn_gap`) into 6 equal slots where `btn_gap` is `max(gutter * 0.75, 8.0)` reduced only if needed so every slot stays at least `min_hit * 0.85` (and never below 48 pixels). Each button fills its slot along the long axis and the full cross-axis of `dock_rect` inset by 4 pixels on each side.
Next, place the layout pods inside `stage_rect` (`sx = stage_rect.x`, `sy = stage_rect.y`, `sw = stage_rect.w`, `sh = stage_rect.h`, `g = gutter`). Let `k_left` be 1 if `swap_map_media` else 0, and `k_right` be 0 if `swap_map_media` else 1.
- Layout 0 (`TWIN_CHRONO`): If `portrait`, stack top pod (`k_left`, circle, 42 percent of `sh - 2*g`), middle row of 3 equal circular pods (`speed`, `weather`, `apps`, 20 percent of `sh - 2*g`), and bottom pod (`k_right`, circle, remaining height). Otherwise (landscape), place left circular pod (`k_left`, width `(sw - mid_w - 2*g) * 0.5`), center column of width `clamp(sh * 0.30, 96.0, 156.0)` split vertically into circular `speed` and `weather` pods with gap `g`, and right circular pod (`k_right`, same width as left).
- Layout 1 (`SOLAR_ORBIT`): If `portrait`, top circular map (56 percent of `sh - g`), bottom row split into left column (`speed` + `weather` circles, 38 percent width) and right circular `media` (62 percent width). Otherwise (landscape), left column (22 percent of `sw - 2*g`, stacked circular `speed` and `weather`), center circular `map` (48 percent of `sw - 2*g`), and right column (30 percent of `sw - 2*g`, stacked circular `media` 60 percent and circular `apps` 40 percent).
- Layout 2 (`ORB_CENTER`): If `portrait`, circular `map` (52 percent of `sh - 2*g`), capsule `media` (24 percent), and bottom row of circular `speed`, `weather`, `apps` (24 percent). Otherwise, left column (21 percent, circular `speed` + `weather`), center circular `map` (44 percent), and right sculpted `media` (35 percent, shape 0).
- Layout 3 (`HORIZON_DIALS`): Full-bleed `map` (`stage_rect`, shape 0), plus floating circular `speed` and `weather` dials of size `clamp(min(sw, sh) * 0.24, 84.0, 128.0)` anchored bottom-left inset by 12 pixels, and floating circular `media` dial of size `clamp(min(sw, sh) * 0.44, 136.0, 224.0)` anchored bottom-right inset by 12 pixels.
- Layout 4 (`HEX_COCKPIT`): If `portrait`, chamfered hex `map` (57 percent of `sh - g`) over chamfered hex `media` (43 percent). Otherwise, 3 chamfered hex pods across `sw - 2*g`: `k_left` (46 percent), `k_right` (34 percent), and `widgets` (20 percent).
- Layout 5 (`CAPSULE_DECK`): Top capsule `map` (64 percent of `sh - g`). Bottom row (36 percent): if `portrait`, single capsule `media`; otherwise capsule `media` (64 percent of `sw - 2*g`) beside circular `speed` (18 percent) and circular `weather` (18 percent).
- Layout 6 (`ASYM_TRIPTYCH`): If `portrait`, `map` (56 percent) over `media` (65 percent width) + stacked `speed`/`weather` circles (35 percent width). Otherwise, 3 columns across `sw - 2*g`: `k_left` (51 percent, shape 0), `k_right` (31 percent, shape 0), and right column (18 percent) stacked with circular `speed`, `weather`, and `apps`.
- Layout 7 (`TRI_COCKPIT`): If `portrait`, `map` (54 percent) over `media` (28 percent) over `widgets` (18 percent). Otherwise, 3 rectangular pods: `k_left` (48 percent), `k_right` (32 percent), `widgets` (20 percent).
- Layout 8 (`SPLIT`): If `portrait`, 55 percent `k_left` over 45 percent `k_right`. Otherwise, 55 percent `k_left` beside 45 percent `k_right` (both rect).
- Layout 9 (`FULL_MAP`, or any other value): Single rectangular `map` pod filling `stage_rect`.
Function `validate_cockpit` takes a `CockpitPlan` and returns 0 if every button is inside `dock_rect`, no two buttons overlap, every button has width and height at least 48 pixels, `dock_rect` and `stage_rect` do not overlap, and every pod lies inside `stage_rect`; otherwise return a nonzero error code (1 button out of dock, 2 buttons overlap, 3 button too small, 4 dock overlaps stage, 5 pod out of stage).
